<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - July 24.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - July 24.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Xerox Corp posted second quarter earnings of $0.94 per share, up from $0.81 a year earlier and a First Call consensus estimate of $0.89. Revenues rose to $4.36 billion from $4.21 billion. The stock closed at 80.</p>
<p>-- Digital Equipment Corp reported a fiscal fourth quarter profit of $0.75 per share, compared to a year-earlier loss of $2.87, which included $492 million in restructuring charges. The First Call consensus estimate was $0.73 per share. The company also announced plans to buy back up to 15 million shares. Digital closed at 40.</p>
<p>-- Avid Technology Inc reported a second quarter profit of $0.27 per share, compared to a loss of $0.17 a year earlier. The stock last traded at 26-5/8.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk 212-859-1730))</p>
